data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"With the centred matrix Xc and the centred target yc, the slopes solve (Xcᵀ Xc + α I) β = Xcᵀ yc. Then the\nintercept is ȳ − x̄ᵀβ. With α > 0 the matrix is positive definite, so a dependent design is still solvable.\nWith α = 0 the design must have full column rank, so check `np.linalg.matrix_rank` on the centred X first."},"hints_note":null}

